      "content": "Gotcha. So if we look at specific urban centers, would we see higher risk scores in neighborhoods where there's a lot of ethnic or racial diversity/shift happening? I'm trying to figure out if the model would naturally flag minority-heavy areas as \"volatile\" more often because of how those migration patterns look compared to, say, more homogenous suburban areas.",
